'' A FIELD LIST OVER A TYPE WITH BITFIELDS, at run time -- 'dim as T z = ( 1, k )', 'x = type<T>( ... )',
'' '*p = type<T>( ... )' -- zeroes the object and stores each field by position, a bitfield by
'' read-modify-write (fbc's structs/bitfield_init.bas). tiko copied a tuple layout instead: '1 0'
'' where fbc prints '1 5', silently, inside a procedure. Expected output is fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/bitfield-list-init.bas -o tests/codegen/bitfieldlistinit.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/bitfieldlistinit.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 0171           7A            A
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 151
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 15
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 06
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 19
